  {
    "id": 11,
    "skill_domain": "Semantic Entailment Detection",
    "thought": "NLI tasks require determining whether a hypothesis is entailed by, contradicted by, or neutral with respect to a premise. The hard cases are: (1) partial entailments where the hypothesis over-generalizes a specific claim, (2) lexical traps where a synonym changes scope, (3) pragmatic implicatures that are true in conversational but not logical context.",
    "eval_relevance": "SNLI, MultiNLI, and ANLI score label accuracy on entailment/contradiction/neutral."
  },
  {
    "id": 12,
    "skill_domain": "Code Correctness Verification",
    "thought": "Code generation evals (HumanEval, MBPP, SWE-bench) run generated code against hidden test cases. The model must mentally simulate execution against edge cases it cannot see: empty inputs, boundary values, type mismatches, off-by-one errors. This requires not just generating plausible code but adversarially probing its own output for failure modes.",
    "eval_relevance": "Pass@k metrics measure whether at least one of k samples passes all hidden tests."
