  {
    "id": 13,
    "skill_domain": "Coreference Resolution",
    "thought": "Pronoun resolution in long texts requires tracking the most recent valid antecedent for each pronoun against gender, number, and semantic plausibility constraints. Hard cases arise when the most syntactically proximate noun is not the semantically correct referent. Winograd schemas are explicitly designed to make syntactic and semantic signals conflict.",
