    "thought": "Analogy completion (A:B :: C:?) requires identifying the structural relationship between A and B, then finding D such that C:D instantiates the same relationship. The failure mode is surface similarity — selecting D that is most similar to B rather than most structurally related to C. The skill is relation extraction independent of object-level similarity.",
    "eval_relevance": "SAT analogies, ARC, and abstract reasoning benchmarks score relational accuracy."
