  {
    "id": 21,
    "skill_domain": "Negation Handling",
    "thought": "Negation is syntactically local but semantically global. 'The patient showed no improvement in any of the three measured outcomes' negates all three simultaneously. Hard cases: double negation ('not without merit'), negative polarity items ('any'), and implicit negation through contradiction ('she arrived before the package, which was already gone').",
    "eval_relevance": "Models consistently underperform on negated versions of factual QA tasks."
