  {
    "id": 22,
    "skill_domain": "Scope Disambiguation",
    "thought": "Quantifier scope determines truth conditions. 'Every student read a book' has two readings: one book for all (wide scope existential) or each student read some book (narrow scope). In formal reasoning tasks, the correct reading is determined by context. Misassigning scope produces logically correct reasoning on the wrong interpretation.",
    "eval_relevance": "Formal semantics and logical reasoning benchmarks test scope sensitivity."
