  {
    "id": 25,
    "skill_domain": "Bias Detection and Neutralization",
    "thought": "BBQ, WinoBias, and similar benchmarks inject demographic correlations to test whether model predictions are driven by group membership rather than evidential content. The skill is computing the answer from the stated evidence alone, with group membership treated as irrelevant noise. A biased model will produce different answers to semantically identical questions differing only in named demographic.",
