Key technical fixes before we implement:

125M params is not 125MB in practice.
Memory depends on dtype (fp16, bf16, fp32) plus optimizer states and KV cache.

For “random init” use config-based construction, not from_pretrained(...).
from_pretrained loads learned weights by default.

Freezing “Layer 1” in HF models means freezing specific module params (e.g. first transformer block), not a single layer1 object in most architectures.

Extending to 128k context is not just changing max_position_embeddings.
You also need compatible positional encoding strategy (e.g. RoPE scaling/long-context training changes) and validation.

“Parallel Unity instances learn simultaneously” is only true during training.
Inference across 4 sims does not update weights unless you run a gradient update loop.

Daily LoRA updates need replay/regularization to avoid drift and forgetting.
Keep eval checkpoints and rollback points.

“CAS near 1.0 because frozen Layer 1” is a hypothesis, not guaranteed.
You’ll need a measured benchmark protocol.

