### 5.1 Core Definition & Purpose
The GPU-Cluster Spawn Pathway is the secure, telemetry-aware handoff mechanism that allows a kernel (after Disciplines 1–4 pass) to detect available higher-capability GPU/Neural Engine resources and atomically transfer or fork execution to them.  
It supports three targets:  
- Local Mac Studio / MacBook M5 Ultra (unified memory cluster)  
- Private Cloud Compute GPU fleet (H100/A100-class or Apple Silicon cloud nodes)  
- Hybrid multi-node clusters  

Goal: Zero perceptible interruption to the user while scaling from 0.6 t/s on iPhone Air to 45+ t/s on cluster.

### 5.2 Detection Phase (Real-Time Resource Discovery)
```swift
class GPUClusterDetector {
    static func discoverAvailableTargets() async -> [SpawnTarget] {
        var targets: [SpawnTarget] = []

        // 1. Local Continuity Devices (Macs on same Apple ID)
        if let nearbyMacs = await ContinuitySession.discoverDevices() {
            for device in nearbyMacs where device.hasM5Ultra && device.unifiedRAMGB >= 96 {
                targets.append(.localMac(id: device.id, estimatedLatencyMs: 4))
            }
        }

        // 2. Private Cloud Compute (attested)
        if PCCEligibility.isAvailable {
            let cloudNodes = await PrivateCloudCompute.fetchEligibleClusters(minTOPS: 1200)
            targets.append(contentsOf: cloudNodes.map { .cloud(clusterID: $0.id, bandwidthGbps: $0.linkSpeed) })
        }

        // 3. Manual / Saved Clusters
        targets += loadSavedClustersFromKeychain()

        // Filter by current telemetry
        return targets.filter { $0.projectedSpeedGain(currentTelemetry) > 8.0 }
    }
}
