### 5.5 Production Implementation – Core Handoff Function (Swift 6)
```swift
@MainActor
func spawnToGPUCluster(currentSession: LanguageModelSession, decision: SpawnDecision) async throws -> RemoteKernelHandle {
    let targets = await GPUClusterDetector.discoverAvailableTargets()
    guard let bestTarget = targets.first else { throw SpawnError.noViableTarget }

    // Phase 1-2: Negotiation
    let negotiation = try await bestTarget.negotiateCapabilities(with: TelemetryNavigator.shared.snapshot())

    // Phase 3: Secure Session
    let remoteSession = try await FoundationModels.createCrossDeviceSession(
        target: bestTarget,
        attestation: generateAttestedPayload()
    )

    // Phase 4: State Transfer
    let kvPrefix = await currentSession.exportKVCachePrefix(maxTokens: 8192)
    try await remoteSession.importState(context: currentSession.context, kvPrefix: kvPrefix)

    // Phase 5-6: Cutover
    await currentSession.suspendAndHandover(to: remoteSession)

    // Start bidirectional telemetry relay
    startTelemetryRelay(from: remoteSession, to: TelemetryNavigator.shared)

    return RemoteKernelHandle(session: remoteSession, target: bestTarget)
}
```

### 5.6 Security & Attestation Model (Critical 2026 Requirements)
- Every handoff uses Secure Enclave + Private Cloud Compute signed attestations.
- Model weights never leave encrypted streams.
- Originating device retains kill-switch (instant session termination).
- Differential privacy on all telemetry sent to cloud.
- Entitlements required: `com.apple.private.foundationmodels.cross-device`, `com.apple.developer.pcc.client`.

### 5.7 iPhone Air 12 GB Specific Optimizations & Edge Cases (28 documented)
